Last week i had the great opportunity to host my own “ Washington State Camp “ for young players from my hometown in Ādaži, Latvia. I had a great time sharing my experience with these young players and explaining the path i had to take to get to where i am today. It was an amazing experience that I hope I can make happen again. Experiences like this is what makes me realize how hard work and dedication pays off. Being able to give back to my community is a big part of who I am, and I feel so blessed I was able to do this. Thank you to my old coach Aigars Nerips and teammates @marcis_osis and @ziemelbriedis for helping me make this happen, and Thank you to the campers that made this experience unforgettable, and to everyone else that helped me put this together. Go Cougs! 

